{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Titanium.UI.MaskedImage",
  "kind": "view",
  "extends": "Titanium.UI.View",
  "inheritanceChain": [
    "Titanium.UI.View",
    "Titanium.Proxy"
  ],
  "platforms": [
    "android",
    "iphone",
    "ipad",
    "macos"
  ],
  "since": {
    "android": "7.3.0",
    "iphone": "0.8",
    "ipad": "0.8"
  },
  "summary": "A control that displays an image composited with a background image or color.",
  "description": "This is a control that can be used to display an image combined with\nanother image and/or color. The layers are drawn in the following order:\n\n* The `mask`, or background image.\n* The `image`, or foreground image.\n* The `tint`, or constant tint color.\n\nThe way the layers are combined depends on the value of the `mode` property.\nThe `mode` value can be set to one of the [Titanium.UI](api:Titanium.UI) `BLEND_MODE` constants.\nThese constants correspond directly to the blend modes described by Apple and Google here:\n\n[\"Bitmap Images and Image Masks\" in Quartz2D Reference](https://developer.apple.com/library/content/documentation/GraphicsImaging/Conceptual/drawingwithquartz2d/dq_images/dq_images.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP30001066-CH212-TPXREF101)\n\n[\"PorterDuff.Mode\" Android Reference](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/PorterDuff.Mode.html)\n\nWhen compositing two images, the `mask` property specifies the background, or\ndestination (D) image, and the `image` property specifies the foreground, or\nsource (S) layer. For example, to use an image as an alpha mask for another image,\nyou could use the following code:\n\n``` js\nvar imageMask = Titanium.UI.createMaskedImage({\n    mask : 'mask.png', // alpha mask\n    image : 'demo_image.png', // image to mask\n    mode : Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOURCE_OUT\n});\n```\n\nNote that this control lacks many of the features associated with a standard\n[ImageView](api:Titanium.UI.ImageView) control.\n\nUse the [Titanium.UI.createMaskedImage](api:Titanium.UI#createMaskedImage) method to create a masked image view.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Lighten Blend Mode",
      "code": "The following code excerpt blends the background image with the given `tint` color:\n\n``` js\nvar imageMask = Titanium.UI.createMaskedImage({\n    mask : 'demo_image.png', // background image\n    tint: 'red',\n    mode : Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_LIGHTEN,\n});\n```\n"
    }
  ],
  "properties": [
    {
      "name": "image",
      "platforms": [
        "android",
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Image drawn as the Foreground image.",
      "description": "Specify a local file path.\n\nUnlike the standard [ImageView](api:Titanium.UI.ImageView), images **cannot** be specified\nusing a remote URL, [Titanium.Blob](api:Titanium.Blob), or [Titanium.Filesystem.File](api:Titanium.Filesystem.File) object.\n",
      "type": [
        {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "name": "String"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mask",
      "platforms": [
        "android",
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Image drawn as the background image.",
      "description": "Specify a local file path.\n\nUnlike the standard [ImageView](api:Titanium.UI.ImageView), images **cannot** be specified\nusing a remote URL, [Titanium.Blob](api:Titanium.Blob), or [Titanium.Filesystem.File](api:Titanium.Filesystem.File) object.\n",
      "type": [
        {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "name": "String"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mode",
      "platforms": [
        "android",
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Blend mode to use to combine layers.",
      "type": [
        {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "name": "Number"
        }
      ],
      "default": "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOURCE_IN",
      "constants": [
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_CLEAR",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_COLOR",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_COLOR_BURN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_COLOR_DODGE",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_COPY",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DARKEN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DESTINATION_ATOP",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DESTINATION_IN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DESTINATION_OUT",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DESTINATION_OVER",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_DIFFERENCE",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_EXCLUSION",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_HARD_LIGHT",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_HUE",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_LIGHTEN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_LUMINOSITY",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_MULTIPLY",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_NORMAL",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_OVERLAY",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_PLUS_DARKER",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_PLUS_LIGHTER",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SATURATION",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SCREEN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOFT_LIGHT",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOURCE_ATOP",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOURCE_IN",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_SOURCE_OUT",
        "Titanium.UI.BLEND_MODE_XOR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "tint",
      "platforms": [
        "android",
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Color to combine with the image, as a color name or hex triplet.",
      "description": "For information about color values, see the \"Colors\" section of [Titanium.UI](api:Titanium.UI).\n",
      "type": [
        {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "name": "String"
        },
        {
          "kind": "type",
          "name": "Titanium.UI.Color"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
